ion of Sweden and Norway, which culminated in its dissolution in 1905. In 1905, the throne of Norway was transferred to his grandnephew Prince Carl of Denmark under the regnal name Haakon VII. When Oscar died in 1907, he was succeeded in Sweden by his eldest son, Gustaf V.","wp_description":"King of Sweden (1872–1907) and Norway (1872–1905)","wikipedia_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oscar_II","image_lead":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/af/Portr%C3%A4tt_av_Oscar_II_i_amiralsuniform._1900-1907._Foto_Lars_Larsson_%28Cropped%29.jpg","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Portr%C3%A4tt_av_Oscar_II_i_amiralsuniform._1900-1907._Foto_Lars_Larsson_%28Cropped%29.jpg/960px-Portr%C3%A4tt_av_Oscar_II_i_amiralsuniform._1900-1907._Foto_Lars_Larsson_%28Cropped%29.jpg","chat_ready":true,"display_from":1872,"display_to":1907}